  "response": "**VERDICT: REJECT**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: \n`BuggyFileInput` fails baseline accessibility requirements across semantic HTML, state communication, and error handling. The input lacks an accessible name, the visual label is a non-semantic `<div>`, error states are neither linked via `aria-describedby` nor marked with `aria-invalid`, and the dynamic error is silent to assistive technologies. It cannot be approved for production in its current state.\n\n---\n\n### Pre-commitment Predictions\nBefore reviewing the code, the most common accessibility failures in custom file upload components were predicted:\n1. File input lacks an associated `<label>` (visual text inside a `div` or `span` without programmatic binding).\n2. Validation errors render visually but are not associated via `aria-describedby`.\n3. Input lacks `aria-invalid` communication when validation fails.\n4. Dynamic error messages appear without live region / status announcements.\n5. Accepted file types and size limits are not communicated in advance as helper text.\n\n*Result*: All 5 predicted failures are present in the component.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings (Blocks Access)\n\n1. **Missing programmatic accessible name / label association**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-24`\n   - **Element**: `<input type=\"file\" ... />` and `<div>Upload file</div>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users (VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS)\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships - Level A), SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A), SC 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions - Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: `<div>Upload file</div>` is visual text only. Because `<input>` has no `id`, no `aria-label`, no `aria-labelledby`, and is not wrapped in a `<label>`, assistive technologies announce the control only by its native browser default (e.g., *\"Choose File, button\"* on VoiceOver/Chrome). In any multi-field or document upload context, screen reader users cannot determine what file is requested.\n   - **Fix**: Replace `<div>Upload file</div>` with `<label htmlFor=\"file-upload-input\">Upload file</label>` and assign `id=\"file-upload-input\"` to the `<input>`.\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: file_input_missing_accessible_name\nfingerprint: f7a1b89c02d4e511\nsource: BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-24\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1, 4.1.2\nsection_508_fpc_context: E205.4 (WCAG 2.0 SC 1.3.1, 4.1.2 Level A)\nseverity: CRITICAL\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard=LOW, low_vision=LOW, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-24: <div>Upload file</div><input type=\"file\" onChange={handleFileChange} accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\" />\nreproduction_steps:\n  1. Inspect accessibility tree in DevTools or navigate via VoiceOver / NVDA.\n  2. Observe computed accessible name of input is empty or UA fallback (\"Choose File\").\nexpected_behavior: Accessible name computed as \"Upload file\" via associated <label>.\nactual_behavior: Input has no programmatic label; accessible name is null.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings (Significantly Degrades Experience)\n\n1. **Validation error is not programmatically associated with input**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:25-29`\n   - **Element**: `<div className=\"error-message\">{error}</div>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users, low vision users using screen magnification\n   - **WCAG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships - Level A), SC 3.3.1 (Error Identification - Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: The error message rendered on lines 25\u201328 has no `id` and the `<input>` lacks `aria-describedby`. When the input has focus, screen readers will not read the error text upon navigation, leaving users unaware why their submission failed or that an error exists.\n   - **Fix**: Add an `id` to the error container (e.g., `id=\"file-upload-error\"`) and associate it with the input using `aria-describedby={error ? \"file-upload-error\" : undefined}` (or combine with helper text ID if present).\n\n2. **Missing `aria-invalid` attribute on failed validation**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:20-24`\n   - **Element**: `<input type=\"file\" ... />`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users, high-contrast mode / custom style users\n   - **WCAG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A), SC 3.3.1 (Error Identification - Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Assistive technologies rely on `aria-invalid=\"true\"` to explicitly convey to the user that the field contains an invalid value. Without it, screen readers report the control as valid even when an error is present.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-invalid={error ? \"true\" : \"false\"}` to `<input>`.\n\n3. **Silent error occurrence \u2014 no dynamic status announcement**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:25-29`\n   - **Element**: `<div className=\"error-message\">{error}</div>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users, blind users\n   - **WCAG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages - Level AA)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When the user selects an oversized file in the operating system's native file picker dialog and closes the picker, focus returns to the input. Because `<div className=\"error-message\">` has no `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live=\"polite\"` container, the error message is never broadcast upon appearance. The user assumes the file was accepted.\n   - **Fix**: Add `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live=\"polite\"` to the error message container (ensuring the live region exists in the DOM or announces reliably).\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: file_input_silent_unassociated_error\nfingerprint: e839a044b11f7c32\nsource: BuggyFileInput.jsx:20-29\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.1, 4.1.2, 4.1.3\nsection_508_fpc_context: E205.4 (WCAG 2.0 SC 3.3.1, 4.1.2 Level A)\nseverity: MAJOR\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard=LOW, low_vision=MEDIUM, cognitive=HIGH\nevidence: BuggyFileInput.jsx:20-29: <input ... /> {error && <div className=\"error-message\">{error}</div>}\nreproduction_steps:\n  1. Select a file > 5MB.\n  2. Native file dialog closes and returns focus to browser window.\n  3. Screen reader remains silent; no error announcement; input state is not invalid.\nexpected_behavior: AT announces error message immediately (via live region/alert) and identifies input as invalid upon focus.\nactual_behavior: DOM renders error silently; input has no aria-invalid or aria-describedby.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings (Friction / Sub-optimal Experience)\n\n1. **Input constraints (size limit & allowed types) not exposed prior to interaction**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:9, 23`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Cognitive accessibility, low vision, screen reader users\n   - **WCAG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions - Level A)\n   - **Why this matters**: The component enforces a 5MB size limit (`file.size > 5000000`) and format restrictions (`accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\"`), but never provides visible or accessible instructions to the user beforehand. Users only discover the size constraint after an upload failure.\n   - **Fix**: Add visible instruction text (e.g., `<p id=\"file-upload-hint\">Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX (Max 5MB)</p>`) and reference it in `aria-describedby=\"file-upload-hint\"`.\n\n2. **Non-actionable error message text**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:10` (`setError('File too large')`)\n   - **Impacted Group**: Cognitive accessibility, all users\n   - **WCAG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.3 (Error Suggestion - Level AA)\n   - **Why this matters**: \"File too large\" indicates a failure but does not explain how to correct it (what the maximum file size is).\n   - **Fix**: Update message to: `\"File exceeds the maximum allowed size of 5MB. Please choose a smaller file.\"`\n\n---\n\n### Enhancements (Best Practice)\n\n1. **DOM value reset on rejected selection**:\n   When validation fails, `e.target.value` is not cleared. If a user attempts to select the exact same file again after fixing or re-attempting, the browser's native `onChange` may not trigger. Clearing `e.target.value = ''` upon rejection ensures reliable re-triggering.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing (Gap Analysis)\n\n- **Missing Semantic Association**: No `<label htmlFor=\"...\">` linkage.\n- **Missing State Semantics**: No `aria-invalid` when `error !== null`.\n- **Missing Contextual Linkage**: No `aria-describedby` connecting the input to either helper instructions or error messages.\n- **Missing Dynamic Announcement**: No `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live` region to notify AT when client-side validation fails.\n- **Missing Upfront Instructions**: No text stating the 5MB size limit or acceptable extensions.\n\n---\n\n### Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|:---|:---:|:---|\n| **Screen reader** | **HIGH** | Unnamed file input; silent dynamic error; no `aria-invalid` or `aria-describedby`. |\n| **Keyboard-only** | **LOW** | Native `<input type=\"file\">` is natively operable via Tab and Space/Enter. |\n| **Low vision** | **MEDIUM** | Error message styling & contrast not guaranteed; no proximity guarantee. |\n| **Cognitive** | **HIGH** | Hidden 5MB constraint discovered only after failure; cryptic error string. |\n| **Vestibular & motion** | **LOW** | No animations or transitions. |\n| **Auditory access** | **LOW** | No audio or video content. |\n| **Environmental contrast** | **MEDIUM** | Ensure `.error-message` color has at least 4.5:1 text contrast. |\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen reader user**: Completely blinded. The input announces without context as an anonymous file picker. If a file over 5MB is chosen, the file picker closes and the user is told nothing.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Native browser keyboard navigation works (Tab reaches the button, Space/Enter opens the OS picker), but after selecting an invalid file, there is no focus indication or automated notification that the selection was rejected.\n- **Low vision user**: If magnifying the screen to the file button area, an error appearing below or displaced may not be noticed without programmatic cues or clear visual proximity.\n- **Cognitive accessibility**: Users are subjected to trial-and-error due to absence of format and size limit guidelines prior to selection.\n\n---\n\n### Realist Check & Severity Calibration\n\n- *Label absence*: A file input with no name in a form cannot be completed with certainty by a non-sighted user. Rated **CRITICAL** (complete loss of context).\n- *Missing `aria-describedby` / `aria-invalid` / announcement*: Rated **MAJOR**. While the user might theoretically discover the error by virtual cursor exploration, normal form completion flow is broken silently.\n- *Instructions & error specificity*: Rated **MINOR**. Workaround exists (trial and error, though frustrating).\n\n---\n\n### Remediation Code\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useId } from 'react';\n\nconst AccessibleFileInput = () => {\n  const [selectedFile, setSelectedFile] = useState(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n\n  const inputId = useId();\n  const hintId = `${inputId}-hint`;\n  const errorId = `${inputId}-error`;\n\n  const handleFileChange = (e) => {\n    const file = e.target.files?.[0];\n    if (file && file.size > 5000000) {\n      setError('File exceeds the maximum allowed size of 5MB. Please choose a smaller file.');\n      setSelectedFile(null);\n      e.target.value = ''; // Reset native input so change event fires if re-attempted\n    } else if (file) {\n      setSelectedFile(file);\n      setError(null);\n    }\n  };\n\n  const describedBy = [\n    hintId,\n    error ? errorId : null\n  ].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-upload\">\n      <label htmlFor={inputId}>\n        Upload file\n      </label>\n\n      <p id={hintId} className=\"help-text\">\n        Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX (Maximum size: 5MB)\n      </p>\n\n      <input\n        id={inputId}\n        type=\"file\"\n        onChange={handleFileChange}\n        accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\"\n        aria-invalid={error ? \"true\" : \"false\"}\n        aria-describedby={describedBy || undefined}\n      />\n\n      {/* Live region for dynamic screen reader announcement */}\n      <div \n        id={errorId} \n        className=\"error-message\" \n        role=\"alert\" \n        aria-live=\"assertive\"\n      >\n        {error}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default AccessibleFileInput;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n\n**Verdict: REJECT**.\nThe component violates WCAG 2.2 Level A criteria (1.3.1, 4.1.2, 3.3.1, 3.3.2). Core functionality is completely broken for screen reader users due to an unassociated label and silent, unassociated error handling. To upgrade to **ACCEPT**, implement native `<label htmlFor>` association, bind `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`, introduce helper instructions for size/type limits, and ensure dynamic errors are announced.\n\n### Open Questions (Unscored)\n1. Will this component be integrated into a larger form submit flow? If so, consider whether form submission should also block and focus this input if empty or invalid.\n2. Is a file preview / removal button required once a valid file is selected? (If so, ensure the remove button has an accessible label such as `\"Remove [filename]\"`).\n",
